Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["CanonicalRuleForm", "ObjectName",
 CellID->528940138,ExpressionUUID->"75b583ec-102b-4b4e-af1c-d275e3c20a64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"4b03c9a5-b2eb-674b-92ea-7e8d99c1766b"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["CanonicalRuleForm",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->
     "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/CanonicalRuleForm"]\
, 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"lhs", " ", "->", " ", "rhs"}], "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f006dfe9-57f9-8c43-94e8-7ac7ac2cd3d6"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the canonical form of a hypergraph rewrite rule in the active \
edge-symmetry universe.",
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["CanonicalRuleForm",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->
     "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/CanonicalRuleForm"]\
, 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"rule1", ",", " ", "rule2", ",", " ", "..."}], "}"}], "]"}]}]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"652db7ec-240a-d84a-80cc-4899f5f24fba"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the canonical form of an unordered rule set: its sorted canonical \
member rules, duplicates removed.",
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"acae38c5-facf-4448-9895-07441ea66e41"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["CanonicalRuleForm",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->
     "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/CanonicalRuleForm"]\
, 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"rule", ",", " ", "universe"}], "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"0baf9e03-190a-ff48-8b31-7cec1b288132"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "and `CanonicalRuleForm[rule, universe, backend]` select the universe and \
the canonical-form backend.",
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["CanonicalRuleForm",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->
     "paclet:SamuelFrerichs/StructureAdaptiveEvolution/ref/CanonicalRuleForm"]\
, 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"rule", ",", " ", "\"\<Declared\>\"", ",", " ", "groups"}], 
    "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a2ccca4b-105d-5e4d-bb5d-c38748f3ebd5"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "uses declared slot-symmetry groups."
}], "Usage",
 CellID->732992262,ExpressionUUID->"321dc0e3-8906-f74a-b90c-99b87e3f24c6"],

Cell["\<\
Two rules have the same canonical form exactly when one becomes the other by \
renaming variables (and, in the unordered universe, reordering edges and \
slots). The left- and right-hand sides are labelled together, so variables \
shared by both sides stay shared.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->824179779,ExpressionUUID->"f4845a66-4f09-9646-95d9-b4732d26ee4c"],

Cell["\<\
In the unordered universe states are simple hypergraphs, so duplicate \
right-hand edges (also up to slot order) cannot change any evolution: rules \
that differ only by them have one canonical form. Left-hand duplicates are \
kept, because they change whether a rule matches. The ordered and declared \
universes keep every multiplicity.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->333342702,ExpressionUUID->"8b75e39d-ea00-3a40-b2d8-d349c7bc3701"],

Cell["\<\
Each rule of a rule set has its own variables; any member rule can fire. The \
canonical identity of a rule set ignores the order and multiplicity of its \
members.\
\>", "Notes",
 CellID->65275482,ExpressionUUID->"f801b14d-783f-5f42-9f26-974322b8b72e"],

